    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Wrangling V — Creating Target Variable**\n",
        "\n",
        "Now, structural changes aside, I noticed that my original dataset does not contain a single variable that directly answers the question of *\"Can we predict whether a student has passed in the course?\"*\n",
        "\n",
        "The original dataset has grades as G1, G2 & G3, but no variable to determine pass status.\n",
        "\n",
        "And so, I use a target variable to transform the final grade (G3) into a binary outcome that represents whether a student passed or failed the course. What metric did I use? I searched the internet and found that in average standard grading conventions, a final grade of 10 or higher represents a passing outcome and so I used that standard.\n",
        "\n",
        "By converting the continuous final grade into a binary variable, I further make the problem suitable for predictive analysis later in this report.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "yxXVquKqu8gB"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "#Create binary target: pass if final grade >= 10\n",
        "students = students.copy()\n",
        "students[\"Passed Final Grade\"] = (students[\"G3\"] >= 10).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "students[\"Passed Final Grade\"].value_counts()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
