      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "((395, 30), (395,))"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "You may ask why I dropped columns G1, G2, G3 & even Passed Final Grade. Here's my explanation: all of them could lead to data leakage and prevent the model from being accurate or unbiased.\n",
        "\n",
        "If any of these columns was used as a predictor, the model would have access to direct information about the outcome it is supposed to predict. For example, Using G3 or Passed Final Grade would be equivalent to giving the model the answer instead of letting it determine accuracy. That'd be biased and would completely undermine the project's findings.\n",
        "\n",
        "Dropping those columns ensures that the model never gets a hint of the final grade, and that predictions are strictly based on the factors that I choose."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ApRU25aKNB9x"
      }
    },
