      "source": [
        "**Plot II: Past Class Failures versus Passed Grade**\n",
        "\n",
        "**Variables Used & Why**:\n",
        "* Passed Class Failures: Past class failures capture academic history, which help understand a pattern if there is one. Unlike study time, this is factual and not self-reported. This is numeric and coded between 0-3.\n",
        "* Passed Final Grade: To measure against. This is binary (pass, 1 or fail, 0).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question Asked**: Does academic history determine future academic performance?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Chart Type**: Used a box plot because it's appropriate for comparing the distribution of a numeric variable across categorical groups."
      ],
