        "**Conclusion**: Students who passed (1) have a median of 0 past failures and the distribution is tightly concentrated at zero. There are very few outliers with multiple past failures. At the same time, students who did not pass (0) have a higher median number of past failures, much wider spread (0 to 3 failures).\n",
        "\n",
        "This highlights that there is a clear separation between the two groups: *Students who pass the final grade almost always have zero past class failures, while students who fail show both higher medians and greater variability in past failures*."
      ],
