      "source": [
        "**Plot III: School Absences versus Passed Grade**\n",
        "\n",
        "**Variables Used & Why**:\n",
        "* School Absences: School absences are a well-known risk factor for poor academic performance. A pattern of absences mean that the student has no engagement or exposure to the material being taught. This is also not self-reported and is numeric.\n",
        "* Passed Final Grade: To measure against. This is binary (pass, 1 or fail, 0).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question Asked**: How severely does school absence affect academic performance? Notice that here, I'm not asking if school absence affects performance, I'm measuring the intensity instead.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Chart Type**: Used a box plot because it's appropriate for comparing the distribution of a numeric variable across categorical groups."
      ],
