      "source": [
        "**Conclusion**: Students who failed have a higher median number of absences, exhibit greater variability and show more extreme high-absence outliers, including very large absence counts. On the other hand, students who passed (Passed Final Grade = 1), tend to have lower median absences and tighter interquartile range. There are outliers, but not enough for a pattern to form.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "So it's safe enough to say that *students with higher numbers of school absences are less likely to pass, while students who pass generally show lower and more stable attendance patterns*."
      ],
