        "# IV(B) Updated Model\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Changed Made & Why**\n",
        "\n",
        "For our second (alternative) model, we will be using a decision tree to test against our first model results. Decision trees capture non-linear relationships and automatically model feature interactions. They are highly interpretable just as well. How? Unlike logistic regression, which fits a single linear boundary, a decision tree learns a sequence of if–then rules that split students into groups with similar outcomes.\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step I: Expanding Features**\n",
        "\n",
        "We add academically and behaviorally relevant variables that are\n",
        "* Clearly interpretable\n",
        "* Available before final grades (those which do not have the risk of Data Leakage)\n",
        "* Visualized in EDA\n",
        "\n",
        "These features are,\n",
        "* Weekly Study Time (individual academic effort)\n",
        "* Past Class Failures (prior academic difficulty)\n",
        "* School Absences (disengagement/risk)\n",
        "* Family Support (home environment)\n",
        "* Workday Alcohol Consumption (weekday behavior)\n",
        "* Weekend Alcohol Consumption (social behavior)\n",
        "* Free Time (time allocation)\n",
        "* Family Relationship Quality (social stability)\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step II**:\n",
        "* Use cross-validation, not a single split\n",
        "* Compare against the Logistic Regression baseline\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step III**: The model itself! (results below)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zIwWiyycvJ4b"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import StratifiedKFold, cross_val_score\n",
        "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
        "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n",
        "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n",
        "from sklearn.dummy import DummyClassifier\n",
        "\n",
        "#Define target and features\n",
        "target_col = \"Passed Final Grade\"\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_cols = [\n",
        "    \"Weekly Study Time\",\n",
        "    \"Past Class Failures\",\n",
        "    \"School Absences\",\n",
        "    \"Family Support\",\n",
        "    \"Workday Alcohol Consumption\",\n",
        "    \"Weekend Alcohol Consumption\",\n",
        "    \"Free Time\",\n",
        "    \"Family Relationship Quality\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "data = students[feature_cols + [target_col]].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "#Ensure binary target\n",
        "data[target_col] = data[target_col].astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "X = data[feature_cols]\n",
        "y = data[target_col]\n",
        "\n",
        "#Preprocessing\n",
        "numeric_features = [\n",
        "    \"Weekly Study Time\",\n",
        "    \"Past Class Failures\",\n",
        "    \"School Absences\",\n",
        "    \"Workday Alcohol Consumption\",\n",
        "    \"Weekend Alcohol Consumption\",\n",
        "    \"Free Time\",\n",
        "    \"Family Relationship Quality\"\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "categorical_features = [\"Family Support\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer(\n",
        "    transformers=[\n",
        "        (\"num\", \"passthrough\", numeric_features),\n",
        "        (\"cat\", OneHotEncoder(drop=\"if_binary\", handle_unknown=\"ignore\"), categorical_features)\n",
        "    ]\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "#Decision Tree model\n",
        "tree_model = Pipeline(steps=[\n",
        "    (\"preprocess\", preprocessor),\n",
        "    (\"classifier\", DecisionTreeClassifier(\n",
        "        max_depth=5,\n",
        "        min_samples_leaf=20,\n",
        "        random_state=42\n",
        "    ))\n",
        "])\n",
        "\n",
        "#Cross-validation\n",
        "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "tree_scores = cross_val_score(\n",
        "    tree_model, X, y, cv=cv, scoring=\"accuracy\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Decision Tree accuracy scores:\", tree_scores)\n",
        "print(f\"Mean accuracy: {tree_scores.mean():.3f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Standard deviation: {tree_scores.std():.3f}\")"
