        "**Interpretation**: The strongest feature by far is **Past Class Failures** with Coefficient at −0.885 & Odds Ratio at 0.41. This means that, if all other variables are constant, each additional past class failure reduces the odds of passing the final grade by about 59% (*since 1 − 0.41 ≈ 0.59*). On the other hand, however, we see that students who reported having **Family Support** have slightly lower odds of passing. This is a point for the limitations of this data, which will be discussed further in the last section of the report. **School Absenses** also contribute to lower grades by 18% odds, while **Weekly Study Time** is the lowest feature that influences the score of a student. It's not to be mistaken as saying \"it doesn't influence\" because the feature does have a positive association, just not a very strong one."
